    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    In this letter, Aline Burch writes on behalf of The Hogarth Press Ltd. to inform William Plomer of a request for a copy of &apos;Sado&apos; by the German publisher Insel-Verlag. She mentions that the publisher may be interested in Plomer's entire body of work and asks whether the company should deal with this request as normal and whether &apos;Sado&apos; is available for Germany.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1951-10-10">
                            10th October, 1951.
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                   
                    <salute>
                        Dear <persName> Mr. Plomer </persName>,
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    We have received a request for a <lb/>
                    reading copy of <title key="novel">SADO</title> from German <lb/>
                    publisher, <orgName key="Q316015"> Insel-Verlag </orgName> of Wiesbaden. The <lb/>
                    request actually comes from <persName key="Q55675211">Dr.L.L.Weltmann</persName> <lb/>
                    who has been asked to keep <orgName>Insel-Verlag</orgName> <lb/>
                    informed of English authors suitable to <lb/>
                    their list. He seems to think there is a <lb/>
                    possibility of them becoming interested in <lb/>
                    your work as a whole. Would you like us <lb/>
                    to deal with this on the usual terms and, <lb/>
                    if so, would you please let me whether <lb/>
                    <title key="novel">SADO</title> is free for Germany?
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        Your sincerely,
                        
                        For <orgName key="Q1623362"> The Hogarth Press <choice> <abbr> Ltd. </abbr> <expan> Limited </expan> </choice> </orgName>
                    </salute>
                    
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName>
                                William Plomer, <choice> <abbr> Esq., </abbr> <expan> Esquire </expan></choice>
                            </persName>
                            
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>
                            29 Linden Gardens,
                            London, W.2.
                        </addrLine>
                    </address>
                   
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
